.Sh DESCRIPTION
Within the library there are two forms of elliptic curve that are of
interest.
The first form is those defined over the prime field Fp.
The elements of Fp are the integers 0 to p-1, where p is a prime number.
This gives us a revised elliptic curve equation as follows:
.Pp
y^2 mod p = x^3 +ax + b mod p
.Pp
The second form is those defined over a binary field F2^m where the
elements of the field are integers of length at most m bits.
For this form the elliptic curve equation is modified to:
.Pp
y^2 + xy = x^3 + ax^2 + b (where b != 0)
.Pp
Operations in a binary field are performed relative to an
.Sy irreducible polynomial .
All such curves with OpenSSL use a trinomial or a pentanomial for this
parameter.
.Pp
Although deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0 and should no longer be used, a
new curve can be constructed by calling
.Fn EC_GROUP_new ,
using the implementation provided by
.Fa meth
(see
.Xr EC_GFp_simple_method 3 )
and associated with the library context
.Fa ctx
(see
.Xr OSSL_LIB_CTX 3 Ns ).
The
.Fa ctx
parameter may be NULL in which case the default library context is used.
It is then necessary to call
.Fn EC_GROUP_set_curve
to set the curve parameters.
Applications should instead use one of the other EC_GROUP_new_*
constructors.
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_new_from_params
creates a group with parameters specified by
.Fa params .
The library context
.Fa libctx
(see
.Xr OSSL_LIB_CTX 3 )
and property query string
.Fa propq
are used to fetch algorithms from providers.
.Fa params
may be either a list of explicit params or a named group, The values for
.Fa ctx
and
.Fa propq
may be NULL. The
.Fa params
that can be used are described in
.Xr EVP_PKEY-EC 7 .
.Pp
EC_GROUP_to_params creates an OSSL_PARAM array with the corresponding
parameters describing the given EC_GROUP. The resulting parameters may
contain parameters describing a named or explicit curve depending on the
EC_GROUP. The library context
.Fa libctx
(see
.Xr OSSL_LIB_CTX 3 )
and property query string
.Fa propq
are used to fetch algorithms from providers.
.Fa bnctx
is an optional preallocated BN_CTX (to save the overhead of allocating
and freeing the structure in a loop).
The values for
.Fa libctx ,
.Fa propq
and
.Fa bnctx
may be NULL. The caller is responsible for freeing the OSSL_PARAM
pointer returned.
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_new_from_ecparameters
will create a group from the specified
.Fa params
and
.Fn EC_GROUP_new_from_ecpkparameters
will create a group from the specific PK
.Fa params .
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_set_curve
sets the curve parameters
.Fa p ,
.Fa a
and
.Fa b .
For a curve over Fp
.Fa p
is the prime for the field.
For a curve over F2^m
.Fa p
represents the irreducible polynomial - each bit represents a term in
the polynomial.
Therefore, there will either be three or five bits set dependent on
whether the polynomial is a trinomial or a pentanomial.
In either case,
.Fa a
and
.Fa b
represents the coefficients a and b from the relevant equation
introduced above.
.Pp
.Xr EC_group_get_curve 3
obtains the previously set curve parameters.
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_set_curve_GFp
and
.Fn EC_GROUP_set_curve_GF2m
are synonyms for
.Fn EC_GROUP_set_curve .
They are defined for backwards compatibility only and should not be
used.
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_get_curve_GFp
and
.Fn EC_GROUP_get_curve_GF2m
are synonyms for
.Fn EC_GROUP_get_curve .
They are defined for backwards compatibility only and should not be
used.
.Pp
The functions
.Fn EC_GROUP_new_curve_GFp
and
.Fn EC_GROUP_new_curve_GF2m
are shortcuts for calling
.Fn EC_GROUP_new
and then the
.Fn EC_GROUP_set_curve
function.
An appropriate default implementation method will be used.
.Pp
Whilst the library can be used to create any curve using the functions
described above, there are also a number of predefined curves that are
available.
In order to obtain a list of all of the predefined curves, call the
function
.Fn EC_get_builtin_curves .
The parameter
.Fa r
should be an array of EC_builtin_curve structures of size
.Fa nitems .
The function will populate the
.Fa r
array with information about the built-in curves.
If
.Fa nitems
is less than the total number of curves available, then the first
.Fa nitems
curves will be returned.
Otherwise the total number of curves will be provided.
The return value is the total number of curves available (whether that
number has been populated in
.Fa r
or not).
Passing a NULL
.Fa r ,
or setting
.Fa nitems
to 0 will do nothing other than return the total number of curves
available.
The EC_builtin_curve structure is defined as follows:
.Bd -literal
 typedef struct {
        int nid;
        const char *comment;
        } EC_builtin_curve;
.Ed
.Pp
Each EC_builtin_curve item has a unique integer id
.Pf ( Fa nid Ns ),
and a human readable comment string describing the curve.
.Pp
In order to construct a built-in curve use the function
.Fn EC_GROUP_new_by_curve_name_ex
and provide the
.Fa nid
of the curve to be constructed, the associated library context to be
used in
.Fa ctx
(see
.Xr OSSL_LIB_CTX 3 )
and any property query string in
.Fa propq .
The
.Fa ctx
value may be NULL in which case the default library context is used.
The
.Fa propq
value may also be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_new_by_curve_name
is the same as
.Fn EC_GROUP_new_by_curve_name_ex
except that the default library context is always used along with a NULL
property query string.
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_free
frees the memory associated with the EC_GROUP. If
.Fa group
is NULL nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_clear_free
is deprecated: it was meant to destroy any sensitive data held within
the EC_GROUP and then free its memory, but since all the data stored in
the EC_GROUP is public anyway, this function is unnecessary.
Its use can be safely replaced with
.Fn EC_GROUP_free .
If
.Fa group
is NULL nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_EC_curve_nid2name
converts a curve
.Fa nid
into the corresponding name.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
All EC_GROUP_new* functions return a pointer to the newly constructed
group, or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn EC_get_builtin_curves
returns the number of built-in curves that are available.
.Pp
.Fn EC_GROUP_set_curve_GFp ,
.Fn EC_GROUP_get_curve_GFp ,
.Fn EC_GROUP_set_curve_GF2m ,
.Fn EC_GROUP_get_curve_GF2m
return 1 on success or 0 on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_EC_curve_nid2name
returns a character string constant, or NULL on error.
